{
  "uid": "secvf-containment",
  "title": "SecVF · Containment & boundary violations",
  "description": "Indicators that SecVF's isolation boundaries (hypervisor, network, filesystem, IPC) may have been crossed. See https://secvf.daxxsec.tech/wiki/Containment-Breakout for response procedures.",
  "tags": ["secvf", "containment", "security"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": { "from": "now-24h", "to": "now" },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Hypervisor anomalies",
      "description": "Unexpected SecVF child processes, VZ crashes, kernel panics in guest. 0 is normal.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [{
        "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"vm-lifecycle\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[24h]))",
        "refId": "A"
      }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "value": null, "color": "green" },
            { "value": 1, "color": "red" }
          ]}
        }
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Network boundary violations",
      "description": "Switch drops, malformed frames, outbound traffic from VMs in Virtual mode (should be zero).",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [{
        "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"network\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[24h]))",
        "refId": "A"
      }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "value": null, "color": "green" },
            { "value": 1, "color": "red" }
          ]}
        }
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Filesystem boundary",
      "description": "Foreign file appearance in bundles, NVRAM mutation outside boot, FSEvents anomalies.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [{
        "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"fsevents\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[24h]))",
        "refId": "A"
      }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "value": null, "color": "green" },
            { "value": 1, "color": "red" }
          ]}
        }
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "IPC anomalies",
      "description": "vsock protocol violations, oversized messages, VirtioFS symlink escapes.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [{
        "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=~\"ai-sandbox|vsock|virtiofs\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[24h]))",
        "refId": "A"
      }],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "value": null, "color": "green" },
            { "value": 1, "color": "red" }
          ]}
        }
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Boundary events over time (by layer)",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"vm-lifecycle\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "A", "legendFormat": "hypervisor"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"network\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "B", "legendFormat": "network"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=\"fsevents\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "C", "legendFormat": "filesystem"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({stream=\"security\", subsystem=~\"ai-sandbox|vsock|virtiofs\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}[5m]))",
          "refId": "D", "legendFormat": "ipc"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "custom": { "drawStyle": "bars", "stacking": { "mode": "normal" }, "fillOpacity": 70 } }
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 6 }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "All boundary-relevant events (24h, live)",
      "description": "Anything CRITICAL or EMERGENCY across the four boundary subsystems. Treat each line as something to investigate.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "loki" },
      "targets": [{
        "expr": "{stream=\"security\", subsystem=~\"vm-lifecycle|network|fsevents|ai-sandbox|vsock|virtiofs\", severity=~\"CRITICAL|EMERGENCY\"}",
        "refId": "A"
      }],
      "options": { "showTime": true, "wrapLogMessage": true, "sortOrder": "Descending" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 14, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 14 }
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Response procedure",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Any red number above ≥ 1?**\n\n1. **Pause the suspect VM immediately** — VM Library → right-click → Pause. Don't stop, pause; you want the state intact.\n2. **Snapshot the bundle** — `secvf vm snapshot &lt;vm&gt; --as &lt;vm&gt;-incident-$(date +%s)`.\n3. **Export logs** — `cp -r ~/.avf/logs/ ~/incident-bundle-$(date +%F)/`.\n4. **Read** the [Containment Breakout wiki](https://secvf.daxxsec.tech/wiki/Containment-Breakout) for the full per-layer response procedure.\n5. **If the host itself may be compromised:** disconnect from network, full system audit.\n\nDon't delete anything. Don't restart SecVF. Don't `rm -rf` the suspect bundle until forensics is done."
      },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 28 }
    }
  ]
}
